   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`python tools/check.py` now passes. I didn't change any files.\n\nThe first run failed with `KeyError: 'NOTES_HOME'`, because `tools/check.py` reads that environment variable and it wasn't set. The script treats it as the directory for scratch notes. I set it to a fresh temp directory for the run:\n\n```\nexport NOTES_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\"; python tools/check.py\n```\n\nWith that set, the one unit test passed and the 100-character line-length check found nothing.\n\nYou'll need to set `NOTES_HOME` yourself whenever you run the check, or in CI. Nothing in the project sets or documents it. If you'd rather not have to, `check.py` could fall back to a temp directory when it's unset. I haven't made that change.",
